<%= render "shared/public_page_meta",
      title: "About Kula HR | Indian Payroll & HRMS",
      description: "Meet the founder building Kula HR and learn why the product focuses on connected, reviewable payroll and HR workflows for Indian teams.",
      canonical_path: about_path,
      schema_type: "AboutPage" %>

<%= render "home/landing/styles" %>
<%= render "resources/styles" %>
<%= render "home/landing/nav" %>

<main class="resource-page">
  <%= render "resources/hero",
        eyebrow: "About Kula HR",
        headline: "Payroll software should show its working.",
        lede: "Kula HR is an independent product being built in India for growing teams that need employee records, attendance, leave and payroll to agree with one another.",
        stamp: "Founder-led product · Built in India · Contact details published" %>

  <section class="bg-white py-20 sm:py-28">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-14 px-6 lg:grid-cols-[.7fr_1.3fr] lg:px-8">
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-kula-700">The premise</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-950">One dependable line from attendance to net pay.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-7 text-base leading-8 text-stone-600">
        <p>Payroll becomes risky when every hand-off creates another version of the truth. Attendance lives in one file, salary changes in another, deductions in a third, and final bank totals are calculated again.</p>
        <p>Kula HR keeps those decisions connected. The product is designed around visible inputs, explicit month locks, employee-level payroll review and exports generated from approved results.</p>
        <p>It is deliberately specific to Indian payroll. PF, ESI, Professional Tax and TDS are treated as core payroll work—not add-ons hidden behind a generic global HR layer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 py-20 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr]">
        <div class="resource-paper rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-kula-700">Founder</p>
          <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-950">Diwanshu Tyagi</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-stone-600">Founder and product engineer working directly across the payroll model, product experience and customer setup.</p>
          <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/diwanshu-tyagi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="rounded-lg bg-kula-700 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-kula-800">LinkedIn</a>
            <a href="https://www.github.com/dwstyagi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="rounded-lg bg-white px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-stone-700 ring-1 ring-inset ring-stone-300 hover:bg-stone-50">GitHub</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <% [
            ["Connected by default", "Employee data, attendance, salary history and payroll outputs should not require repeated re-entry."],
            ["Review before automation", "A calculation is only useful when HR can inspect the inputs, exceptions and employee-level result."],
            ["Honest product claims", "Capabilities are described as they work today. Certifications, customers and expert reviews are not implied."],
            ["Useful before signup", "Calculators, calendars, checklists and templates remain publicly available without creating an account."]
          ].each do |title, body| %>
            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6">
              <div class="h-1 w-10 rounded-full bg-marigold-400"></div>
              <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-bold text-stone-900"><%= title %></h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600"><%= body %></p>
            </article>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-kula-950 py-16 text-white sm:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl flex-col justify-between gap-8 px-6 lg:flex-row lg:items-center lg:px-8">
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-marigold-300">A direct line</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Ask the person building the product.</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-kula-100/70">Email hello@kula-hr.com or use the contact form.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="<%= contact_path %>" class="shrink-0 rounded-xl bg-white px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-kula-950 hover:bg-kula-50">Contact Kula HR</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%= render "home/landing/footer" %>
<%= render "marketing_pages/scripts" %>
